  "description": "Annual real (after German inflation) total returns of a 10-year German federal government bond (Bund), the benchmark of euro area government bonds, in euros (Deutsche Mark before 1999). Each year a new 10-year bond is bought at par at December's yield, so its coupon is that yield; a year later it is valued with 9 years left at the next December's yield. nominalReturn = coupon + price - 1; realReturn = (1 + nominalReturn) / (1 + inflation) - 1. This is the constant-maturity method used for US Treasuries by Shiller and Damodaran; it leaves out trading costs and fund fees.",
